6.

Create a styled multi-line code block.
a) Write a simple Python for loop inside the correct preformatted element.
b) Add CSS so the block has a dark background (#1e1e1e), white text, padding, and rounded corners.
c) Use a monospace font.

**ANSWER**

<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">

<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Styled Python Code</title>

    <style>
        pre {
            background-color: #1e1e1e;
            color: white;
            padding: 20px;
            border-radius: 10px;
            font-family: monospace;
        }
    </style>
</head>

<body>

    <pre>
for i in range(5):
    print(i)
    </pre>

</body>

</html>


